      "role": "user",
      "content": "i've already tried all that stuff. the counselors just tell me to cut back on things i can't even cut, and the assistance programs have like six month waiting lists. the math doesn't change though. it's just a permanent deficit. it’s like being on a treadmill that’s slowly speeding up and i'm just waiting for the moment i can't keep my balance anymore. honestly, sometimes i think the only way to actually stop the debt from growing is to just... stop. like, if you aren't part of the equation anymore, the math doesn't matter. does that sound crazy? just feeling like the only logical way out of a deficit is to exit the system entirely.",
